  "enhanced_information": "In this case of suspected organophosphate poisoning presenting with gastrointestinal symptoms, watery diarrhea, garlic-like odor on breath, and QTc prolongation on ECG, the most appropriate administration is Fomepizole, not Physostigmine. Physostigmine is contraindicated in organophosphate poisoning due to the risk of exacerbating cholinergic crisis. Fomepizole is the preferred antidote for toxic alcohol poisoning, including methanol and ethylene glycol, which can present similarly to organophosphate poisoning.",
